-- allium: 3
-- 19-regulatory-reports.allium

-- Scope: Turning signed-off reported figures into the regulator's report
--   files, and following each report until the regulator has answered
--   (D-047).
-- Includes: report templates from configuration, generation and validation
--   of report files, release after sign-off, export, recording of the
--   submission and of the regulator's answer, deadlines, new versions after a
--   restatement with a per-cell difference list.
-- Excludes:
--   - The figures themselves (11) and their sign-off (13): reused as is.
--   - Transmission to a regulator: a person submits the exported file through
--     the regulator's own channel; Veridian holds no regulator credentials
--     and makes no external call (D-047).
--   - The concrete template layouts of each regulator: configuration
--     artefacts (05), transcribed from the regulator's publication.
-- Dependencies: 01, 02, 03, 05, 06, 11, 13.
--
-- Principles (D-047):
--   - A report is a pure function of the reported figures of one publication
--     and one template definition. Nothing is typed in and nothing is
--     recomputed: every cell comes from a ReportedFigure (13), so a report
--     can be rebuilt years later from retained figures and the retained
--     template and must give the same file hash.
--   - The engine is template-agnostic. v1's worked example is the EBA COREP
--     market-risk templates for the simplified standardised approach, C 18.01
--     to C 23.01 (D-052; public taxonomy); PRA, HKMA and US federal
--     templates are added as configuration without changing this spec.
--     Identifiers and cell references are transcribed verbatim from the
--     regulator's publication (extracted in docs/regulatory/
--     eba-corep-market-risk/); the validation rules and the file format
--     remain to be transcribed before the first template is released.
--   - Generation is a calculation node (02): its calc_id covers the template
--     hash and the hashes of the figures it reads.

use "./01-bitemporal-data.allium" as data
use "./02-calculation-graph.allium" as graph
use "./05-configuration-release.allium" as cfg
use "./06-batch-scheduling.allium" as batch
use "./11-frtb-sa.allium" as frtb
use "./12-web-front-end-and-batch-console.allium" as web
use "./13-report-review-alerts-trends.allium" as review

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Contracts
------------------------------------------------------------

contract ReportGeneration {
    generate: (publication_figures: Set<String>, template_hash: String, previous_report_hash: String?) -> String
    validate: (report_hash: String, template_hash: String) -> String

    @invariant CellsFromReportedFigures
        -- Every cell value is a reported figure of the publication (13), or a
        -- sum or other arithmetic of reported figures that the template
        -- states. A cell the figures cannot supply is a deterministic
        -- rejection naming the cell; it is never left blank or filled by hand.

    @invariant PrescribedRoundingAtTheEdge
        -- Figures are kept at full precision (13). Rounding to the template's
        -- reporting unit (for example thousands) and its sign convention
        -- happen only here, when the file is produced, exactly as the
        -- regulator prescribes (F-3), and are separate from the canonical
        -- rounding used for hashing (D-015). Totals in the template are
        -- computed from the rounded cells when the regulator's rules require
        -- it, and the template says which.

    @invariant TemplateCurrency
        -- A template names the currency its amounts are reported in. A
        -- perimeter whose reporting currency differs is a deterministic
        -- rejection; there is no conversion at this stage (11, ReportingCurrency).

    @invariant RegulatorRulesBlockRelease
        -- The regulator's own validation rules, carried in the template, are
        -- evaluated on the finished file. A rule that fails keeps the report
        -- from release and is listed with the cells involved; a rule the
        -- regulator marks as a warning is listed and does not block.

    @invariant ReproducibleFromRetainedData
        -- Given the same retained figures and the same template definition,
        -- the file is byte-identical and its hash matches the recorded one.
        -- Template definitions are kept as long as the reports built from
        -- them (same retention class as reported figures, 13).

    @invariant DataClassSeparation
        -- A report built from synthetic, test or what-if data is generated
        -- for review but carries its data class in its content and can never
        -- be exported as a regulatory report or recorded as submitted
        -- (D-010).

    @invariant NewVersionCarriesDifferences
        -- A report that restates an earlier one carries, cell by cell, the
        -- earlier and the new value, and lists cells that appear or
        -- disappear. Unchanged cells are not listed.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A regulator's template as the bank uses it, from a configuration release.
-- definition_hash covers the template's cell mapping, rounding and sign
-- rules, validation rules and taxonomy version.
entity ReportTemplate {
    regulator: String
    template_code: String
    taxonomy_version: String
    file_format: xbrl_csv | csv | spreadsheet
    reporting_currency: String
    -- The filing deadline as a number of business days after the reference
    -- date, on the regulator's calendar (03).
    deadline_business_days: Integer
    deadline_calendar: String
    release: cfg/ConfigurationRelease
    definition_hash: String
}

-- One generated report: one template, one perimeter, one publication.
entity RegulatoryReport {
    publication: batch/RunPublication
    template: ReportTemplate
    perimeter: frtb/ReportingPerimeter
    version: Integer
    supersedes: RegulatoryReport?
    file_hash: String
    file_ref: String
    data_class: data/DataClass
    generated_at: Timestamp
    due_at: Timestamp
    state: generated | failed_validation | validated | released | submitted | accepted | refused | superseded

    transitions state {
        generated -> validated
        generated -> failed_validation
        validated -> released
        released -> submitted
        submitted -> accepted
        submitted -> refused
        accepted -> superseded
        refused -> superseded
        released -> superseded
        terminal: failed_validation, superseded
    }
}

-- A validation rule that failed, with the cells it involves.
entity ValidationFinding {
    report: RegulatoryReport
    rule_ref: String
    blocking: Boolean
    cells: String
    description: String
}

-- One cell that differs between a report and the one it supersedes.
entity CellDifference {
    report: RegulatoryReport
    cell_ref: String
    previous_value: Decimal?
    new_value: Decimal?
}

-- A person's export of a released report: who took the file and when.
entity ReportExport {
    report: RegulatoryReport
    exported_by: data/User
    exported_at: Timestamp
    file_hash: String
}

-- The submission made by a person through the regulator's channel.
entity Submission {
    report: RegulatoryReport
    submitted_by: data/User
    submitted_at: Timestamp
    receipt_ref: String
    outcome: pending | accepted | refused
    outcome_at: Timestamp?
    outcome_reason: String?
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    -- How long before a deadline an unsubmitted report is brought to its
    -- owner's attention.
    deadline_warning: Duration = 1.days
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Templates come only from configuration releases, like schedules (06) and
-- perimeters (11).
rule RegisterReleaseTemplates {
    when: cfg/ReleaseActivated(release, previous)
    ensures:
        for d in release_templates(release):
            TemplateDefined(release: release, definition: d)
}

rule CreateTemplate {
    when: TemplateDefined(release, definition)
    requires: not exists ReportTemplate{definition_hash: template_definition_hash(definition)}
    ensures: ReportTemplate.created(
        regulator: template_regulator(definition),
        template_code: template_code_of(definition),
        taxonomy_version: template_taxonomy(definition),
        file_format: template_format(definition),
        reporting_currency: template_currency(definition),
        deadline_business_days: template_deadline_days(definition),
        deadline_calendar: template_deadline_calendar(definition),
        release: release,
        definition_hash: template_definition_hash(definition)
    )
}

-- Every publication of a regulatory schedule gets its reports before sign-off,
-- so the signers see the files they release. A restatement's reports link to
-- the reports of the publication they replace and carry the differences.
rule GenerateReports {
    when: publication: batch/RunPublication.created
    requires: review/is_regulatory(publication.run.schedule)
    ensures:
        for t in templates_applying(publication.run.schedule, publication.run.as_of):
            ReportGenerated(
                publication: publication,
                template: t,
                perimeter: perimeter_of(publication.run.schedule, t),
                previous: report_replaced_by(publication, t)
            )
}

rule CreateReport {
    when: ReportGenerated(publication, template, perimeter, previous)
    requires: template.reporting_currency = perimeter.reporting_currency
    ensures: RegulatoryReport.created(
        publication: publication,
        template: template,
        perimeter: perimeter,
        version: if previous != null: previous.version + 1 else: 1,
        supersedes: previous,
        file_hash: report_file_hash(publication, template),
        file_ref: report_file_ref(publication, template),
        data_class: publication.run.schedule.data_class,
        generated_at: now,
        due_at: report_due_at(template, publication.run.as_of),
        state: generated
    )
}

-- A template whose currency differs from the perimeter's is rejected visibly,
-- never skipped.
rule RejectTemplateCurrencyMismatch {
    when: ReportGenerated(publication, template, perimeter, previous)
    requires: template.reporting_currency != perimeter.reporting_currency
    ensures: review/Alert.created(
        source: run_problem,
        subject_ref: template.template_code,
        description: "template currency differs from the perimeter's reporting currency",
        raised_at: now,
        owner: publication.run.schedule.owner,
        escalated: false,
        alert_state: raised
    )
}

rule ListDifferences {
    when: report: RegulatoryReport.created
    requires: report.supersedes != null
    ensures:
        for d in cell_differences(report, report.supersedes):
            CellDifference.created(
                report: report,
                cell_ref: difference_cell(d),
                previous_value: difference_previous(d),
                new_value: difference_new(d)
            )
}

rule ValidateReport {
    when: report: RegulatoryReport.created
    ensures:
        for f in validation_findings(report):
            ValidationFinding.created(
                report: report,
                rule_ref: finding_rule(f),
                blocking: finding_blocking(f),
                cells: finding_cells(f),
                description: finding_description(f)
            )
        if has_blocking_findings(report):
            report.state = failed_validation
            review/Alert.created(
                source: run_problem,
                subject_ref: report.template.template_code,
                description: "regulatory report failed the regulator's validation rules",
                raised_at: now,
                owner: report.publication.run.schedule.owner,
                escalated: false,
                alert_state: raised
            )
        else:
            report.state = validated
}

-- Release follows the sign-off of the publication (13); a report that failed
-- validation is never released.
rule ReleaseReports {
    when: review/ReportReleased(signoff)
    ensures:
        for r in reports_of(signoff.publication):
            if r.state = validated and r.data_class = production:
                r.state = released
                if r.supersedes != null:
                    ReportSuperseding(previous: r.supersedes)
}

rule SupersedePrevious {
    when: ReportSuperseding(previous)
    requires: previous.state in {released, accepted, refused}
    ensures: previous.state = superseded
}

rule ExportReport {
    when: ReportExportRequested(user, report)
    requires: report.state in {released, submitted, accepted, refused}
    requires: data/permitted(user, "report.export", report.template.template_code)
    requires: data/freshly_authenticated(user)
    ensures: ReportExport.created(
        report: report,
        exported_by: user,
        exported_at: now,
        file_hash: report.file_hash
    )
}

-- The submission is recorded by the person who made it, against a report they
-- exported. The receipt reference is the regulator's own.
rule RecordSubmission {
    when: SubmissionRecorded(user, report, receipt_ref)
    requires: report.state = released
    requires: exists ReportExport{report: report, exported_by: user}
    requires: data/permitted(user, "report.submit", report.template.template_code)
    requires: data/freshly_authenticated(user)
    ensures:
        report.state = submitted
        Submission.created(
            report: report,
            submitted_by: user,
            submitted_at: now,
            receipt_ref: receipt_ref,
            outcome: pending
        )
}

rule RecordAcceptance {
    when: RegulatorAccepted(user, submission)
    requires: submission.outcome = pending
    requires: data/permitted(user, "report.submit", submission.report.template.template_code)
    ensures:
        submission.outcome = accepted
        submission.outcome_at = now
        submission.report.state = accepted
}

-- A refusal is an alert and needs a corrected version: the regulator's reason
-- is kept, and the owner decides on a restatement (06).
rule RecordRefusal {
    when: RegulatorRefused(user, submission, reason)
    requires: submission.outcome = pending
    requires: data/permitted(user, "report.submit", submission.report.template.template_code)
    ensures:
        submission.outcome = refused
        submission.outcome_at = now
        submission.outcome_reason = reason
        submission.report.state = refused
        review/Alert.created(
            source: run_problem,
            subject_ref: submission.report.template.template_code,
            description: "regulator refused the submission",
            raised_at: now,
            owner: submission.report.publication.run.schedule.owner,
            escalated: false,
            alert_state: raised
        )
}

rule DeadlineApproaching {
    when: report: RegulatoryReport.due_at - config.deadline_warning <= now
    requires: report.state in {generated, failed_validation, validated, released}
    ensures: review/Alert.created(
        source: run_problem,
        subject_ref: report.template.template_code,
        description: "regulatory report not yet submitted near its deadline",
        raised_at: now,
        owner: report.publication.run.schedule.owner,
        escalated: false,
        alert_state: raised
    )
}

rule DeadlineMissed {
    when: report: RegulatoryReport.due_at <= now
    requires: report.state in {generated, failed_validation, validated, released}
    ensures: review/Alert.created(
        source: run_problem,
        subject_ref: report.template.template_code,
        description: "regulatory report deadline missed",
        raised_at: now,
        owner: report.publication.run.schedule.owner,
        escalated: false,
        alert_state: raised
    )
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

invariant OnlyProductionIsSubmitted {
    for r in RegulatoryReports:
        r.state in {released, submitted, accepted, refused} implies r.data_class = production
}

invariant NoReleaseWithoutSignOff {
    for r in RegulatoryReports:
        r.state in {released, submitted, accepted, refused}
            implies exists review/ReportSignOff{publication: r.publication, signoff: signed_off}
}

invariant SubmissionNeedsExport {
    for s in Submissions:
        exists ReportExport{report: s.report, exported_by: s.submitted_by}
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

actor ReportingOfficer {
    identified_by: data/User
}

actor ReportWorker {
    identified_by: data/User
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

surface RegulatoryReportHandling {
    facing officer: ReportingOfficer
    context report: RegulatoryReport

    exposes:
        report.template.regulator
        report.template.template_code
        report.template.taxonomy_version
        report.perimeter.name
        report.publication.run.as_of
        report.version
        report.supersedes
        report.state
        report.due_at
        report.file_hash
        findings_of(report)
        differences_of(report)
        submission_of(report)

    provides:
        ReportExportRequested(officer, report) when report.state in {released, submitted, accepted, refused}
        SubmissionRecorded(officer, report, receipt_ref) when report.state = released
        RegulatorAccepted(officer, submission) when submission_of(report).outcome = pending
        RegulatorRefused(officer, submission, reason) when submission_of(report).outcome = pending

    contracts:
        demands web/WebFrontEnd
}

surface ReportGenerationComputation {
    facing worker: ReportWorker

    contracts:
        demands ReportGeneration
        demands graph/DeterministicComputation

    @guarantee GoldenFiles
        -- Golden reports (frozen figures, template and the expected file) are
        -- reproduced byte for byte before a template can enter a production
        -- release (F-1).
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

-- release_templates, template_* accessors: from the release artefacts (05).
-- templates_applying(schedule, as_of): templates of the active release that
--   apply to the schedule on that date (taxonomy versions have effective
--   dates, so a date before a taxonomy switch uses the earlier one).
-- perimeter_of(schedule, template): the perimeter the template reports on.
-- report_replaced_by(publication, template): the report of the publication
--   that this one replaces (06), for the same template and perimeter.
-- report_file_hash, report_file_ref: result of the generation node (02); the
--   file lives in the object store under the retention class of 13.
-- report_due_at(template, as_of): deadline_business_days business days after
--   the reference date on the template's calendar (03).
-- cell_differences, difference_*: cell-by-cell comparison of two reports.
-- validation_findings, finding_*, has_blocking_findings: the regulator's
--   validation rules evaluated on the file.
-- reports_of(publication), findings_of, differences_of, submission_of:
--   queries.
-- Alerts use spec 13's Alert entity directly (source run_problem), owned by the schedule's owner.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Resolved (D-047): template-agnostic engine with the EBA COREP market-risk
-- templates as the worked example; a person submits the exported file; a
-- restatement produces a new linked version with a difference list.
-- Done 2026-11-16: identifiers and cell references of the published EBA
-- market-risk templates (framework 4.0, C(2024) 8389) are extracted verbatim
-- in docs/regulatory/eba-corep-market-risk/. They are the simplified
-- standardised approach (C 18.01 to C 23.01), not the sensitivities-based
-- method of spec 11.
-- Resolved (D-052): the worked example is the simplified standardised
-- approach templates C 18.01 to C 23.01.
-- Resolved (D-052): the figures of C 18.01, C 21.01 and C 22.01 are produced
-- by spec 22 (simplified standardised approach). C 19.01, C 20.01 and C 23.01
-- are not produced in v1 (no v1 instrument attracts them).
open question "When the EBA publishes the FRTB-based templates (release 4.4 mentions them without codes), they are added as configuration; the engine does not change."
-- Done 2026-11-17: the 261 EBA validation rules that name the three
-- templates (4.4 phase 1 workbook) and the filing rules' format sections are
-- extracted verbatim in docs/regulatory/eba-corep-market-risk/. The validation
-- rules are carried in the template definition (see the invariant at line
-- 74, the regulator's own validation rules) as the expressions published,
-- with their severity and module.
open question "The taxonomy's own cell identifiers (the DPM 2.0 database) are still to be transcribed; the validation rules address cells by the templates' row and column codes, so generation can proceed without them."
open question "The EBA filing rules define both xBRL-XML and xBRL-CSV and leave the choice and the file naming to the recipient supervisor. Which does each of the bank's supervisors require? The template's file_format field is set per template and regulator from the answer."
open question "The validation rules and the taxonomy name the tables C_18.00, C_21.00 and C_22.00, while the annex of C(2024) 8389 names them C 18.01, C 21.01 and C 22.01. Which code goes into template_code and the file? The answer comes from the supervisor's reporting instructions."
open question "Which regulators and templates does each legal entity report to, and who owns each template's configuration?"
open question "Filing deadlines and calendars per regulator: configured per template; the bank confirms its own obligations."
-- Resolved (D-054): a corrected version after a refusal is a restatement
-- with four-eyes review (06), a new linked version with a per-cell
-- difference list; the regulator's reason is recorded on the new version.
open question "Retention of the exported files and submission receipts: same 10 years as reported figures, to be confirmed with compliance."
